Patch T9 oracles (rung 1b, task T9; gate G5): the per-frame GPU budgets,
and protection for the shot and video tests.

- budgets.toml gains a [gpu] table (amendments 30 and 40): at most 12
  draws, 12 pipeline switches, 8 bind-group switches and 2,048 uploaded
  bytes per frame, about four times what the testbed's top-down view
  needs. `shot` and `video` hold every frame they render to it with
  `--budgets` (exit 13, [E-BUDGET]): criterion 9 `gpu-report-budgets`.
- crates/game-testbed/tests/shot_video.rs joins protected.toml and
  .github/CODEOWNERS (amendment 41, optional).
- No xtask step: criterion 9's check is the native job's `gpu-budgets`
  step (amendment 42).

Base: main with T9's commit (14ca032). Its lines sit right after
version.rs's, so it applies before or after the other queued oracle
patches. At the repo root, run `git apply` with this file, then
`cargo xtask quick`. Session 17's T9 entry in PROGRESS.md says how it was
tested.
Text before the first `diff --git` line is ignored by `git apply`.

